mid f_i$ such that $$x_{i;t_0}= rac{f_i(x_{1;t},\cdots,x_{n;t})}{{ f x}_t^{d^t(x_{i;t_0})}}.$$ Denote by $F^{ f v}=f_1^{v_1}\cdots f_n^{v_n}$. Since $v_1,\cdots,v_n\in \mathbb Z$, $F^{ f v}$ can be written in the form of $F^{ f v}= rac{F_{1;{ f v}}}{F_{2;{ f v}}}$, where $F_{1;{ f v}}, F_{2;{ f v}}\in \mathbb {NP}[x_{1;t},\cdots,x_{n;t}]$ with $x_{j;t}
